WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.060 --> 00:00:02.620
Hey, Jen!
(Jenna: Yo!)

00:00:02.620 --> 00:00:06.509
Can you make sure I'm in frame? 
Hi guys. I'm at camera camp.

00:00:07.149 --> 00:00:10.979
Am I in frame? (Jenna: Yeah, you are. There's a reflection from this light on the back wall.)

00:00:11.580 --> 00:00:13.060
Disregard that reflection,

00:00:13.280 --> 00:00:17.700
even though I'm in camera camp, you would think this would be the most incredibly shot, beautiful video that you've ever seen.

00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:20.400
But it's not. I'm sitting on the floor in my hotel room.

00:00:20.660 --> 00:00:22.900
This is where we are.
(Jenna: I got you.)

00:00:23.240 --> 00:00:29.640
So what's really cool is, this event is put on by Sony and there's a ton of other influencers and photographers and just really, really cool people.

00:00:29.860 --> 00:00:32.180
And they're also letting you check out and rent gear for the week.

00:00:32.189 --> 00:00:37.769
What I'm filming on right now is the a7R III. I've actually never used this camera before and I'm shooting on a 12-24 lens.

00:00:37.770 --> 00:00:40.439
And it's really cool because it's super wide angle. Watch.

00:00:40.960 --> 00:00:42.560
Did I did I zoom in or out?

00:00:42.560 --> 00:00:43.480
(Jenna: In)

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:45.000
(Jenna: Out)

00:00:45.760 --> 00:00:47.760
Can you zoom me back in to how I had it?

00:00:48.180 --> 00:00:50.160
(Jenna: Pretty good. You are still a little far. You are very small.)

00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:51.980
Yeah, but I've got a lot of things to show them.

00:00:51.980 --> 00:00:53.079
(Jenna: You do . I have to get ready for camera camp.)

00:00:53.079 --> 00:00:54.390
So there's all kinds of cool things

00:00:54.390 --> 00:00:55.829
we're going to be doing for the next couple of days.

00:00:55.829 --> 00:00:58.679
But I wanted to go through some of the gear that I brought because a lot of you guys are always

00:00:58.750 --> 00:01:03.149
asking what I take with me when I travel on trips because it's always a lot of gear.

00:01:03.149 --> 00:01:06.149
It's usually very heavy and to be completely honest with you,

00:01:06.150 --> 00:01:11.939
I hardly ever use everything that I bring. But every time I don't bring something, it's the time that I actually need it.

00:01:11.939 --> 00:01:17.309
So let's go through. The first thing that I want to show you is I got this specifically for this trip.

00:01:17.310 --> 00:01:19.310
I've always wanted to get a gimbal. So what I got

00:01:20.140 --> 00:01:24.269
is a Zhiyun Crane 2 because it can hold up to I think 7 pounds.

00:01:24.270 --> 00:01:27.570
So I figure if I have a heavy lens plus the body plus a microphone pack,

00:01:27.850 --> 00:01:30.089
potentially could easily be 7 pounds, so I got that one.

00:01:30.090 --> 00:01:36.090
I'm most excited about the Ronin-S, but I don't know when that's gonna be out. And I need something in the meantime.

00:01:36.250 --> 00:01:38.339
Especially with E3 coming up, and a bunch of other events.

00:01:38.409 --> 00:01:42.209
So I got the Zhiyun crane, and if you guys have ever seen these things,

00:01:42.209 --> 00:01:44.460
I thought it was gonna be a little bit smaller.

00:01:44.680 --> 00:01:51.500
So, the expectation versus reality. It just came in right before I left for this trip. I didn't even have time to do an unboxing.

00:01:51.780 --> 00:01:55.120
I had to take out half of my clothes.
(Jenna: Another backpack?)

00:01:55.280 --> 00:02:00.120
Yeah, Francesca got me this for my birthday. Isn't this the most beautiful thing you've ever seen?

00:02:00.340 --> 00:02:01.780
Jenna look. 
(Jenna: Oh you are kidding.)

00:02:01.980 --> 00:02:04.160
No, I wasn't kidding. This is half of my suitcase.

00:02:04.160 --> 00:02:08.600
I tried to take it out of the case, but I wanted it to be protected, especially since I just got it.

00:02:09.460 --> 00:02:11.680
Haven't even set it up. I haven't done anything yet.

00:02:11.940 --> 00:02:15.260
It's huge! 
(Jenna: Oh my, I'm not carrying anything!) 
*both laugh*

00:02:15.480 --> 00:02:18.680
I think I probably should had the smaller one. Moving along.

00:02:18.760 --> 00:02:21.510
Okay, first I had to do some rearranging

00:02:21.660 --> 00:02:26.280
because I was gonna try to only bring one backpack and it didn't work, 'cause we're coming to camera camp,

00:02:26.280 --> 00:02:32.550
I thought, I'm gonna want to bring some lenses. But of course the first thing that we've got here is a Mophie charger,

00:02:32.550 --> 00:02:37.580
this is the USB-C one, which I usually specifically use for charging my

00:02:38.290 --> 00:02:45.569
Samsung Galaxy. I've been using the S9, the lilac. And of course the iPhone X. So in these little side pockets

00:02:45.940 --> 00:02:50.700
over on this side, this always gets flagged by TSA. This is a Samson microphone.

00:02:50.700 --> 00:02:54.720
This just folds down, just like so, and then folds right back up.

00:02:54.720 --> 00:03:02.070
So also in this bag I've got, this is a tripod that goes to one of the Insta360 cameras. Here's one of the Joby tripods.

00:03:02.070 --> 00:03:05.180
I just started using this one because if I'm vlogging with heavier lenses,

00:03:05.190 --> 00:03:09.089
I do need to have something else that I can hold onto, so this works a little bit better than the smaller

00:03:09.090 --> 00:03:12.210
Manfrotto ones that I'm always using. Since we're on camera camp,

00:03:12.310 --> 00:03:19.320
I last a minute decided that I was gonna bring some more lenses. This is, oh is the 16-35.

00:03:19.320 --> 00:03:21.599
I love this lens because it is a wide-angle lens.

00:03:21.600 --> 00:03:25.739
But I can also get a little bit of zoom. And the other one that I brought, this one is a fixed lens.

00:03:25.750 --> 00:03:28.200
This is the 18 mm, this is a Zeiss.

00:03:28.209 --> 00:03:33.299
This is what I used to always vlog with, but the problem is you couldn't get any zoom.

00:03:33.300 --> 00:03:36.089
So basically you have this 18 mm and that's it.

00:03:36.120 --> 00:03:39.030
So I really am interested to test out the one that I'm using right now.

00:03:39.030 --> 00:03:41.970
This is one of the rental ones that I got from the event that we're at.

00:03:42.190 --> 00:03:43.740
So we'll see how it looks.

00:03:43.740 --> 00:03:48.420
I know the lighting's not the best, but it's the best that I could do in our cabin-hotel situation.

00:03:48.459 --> 00:03:53.789
This is the a7 III. I got this new little neck strap for it.

00:03:53.790 --> 00:03:56.279
It's one of the ones that have the quick release, so you can just go...

00:03:58.849 --> 00:04:05.379
Moderately quick release. So if I'm vlogging sometimes or going to be using the gimbal I wanted to be able to easily strap...

00:04:05.380 --> 00:04:07.460
*weird noise in the background*
*Jenna giggles*

00:04:07.580 --> 00:04:09.200
I wanted to easily be able to,

00:04:09.460 --> 00:04:10.400
*another noise*
*both giggle*

00:04:10.600 --> 00:04:12.080
... take off these straps.

00:04:12.080 --> 00:04:16.480
This is the microphone that I use on all of these cameras. It's actually the same microphone I'm using no.w

00:04:16.480 --> 00:04:22.749
It's this little Sony one and it's great because you don't have to use any cords or any audio input.

00:04:22.749 --> 00:04:27.660
It uses the hot shoe. So it automatically just works basically like magic. And the lens that I'm using one here,

00:04:27.660 --> 00:04:31.440
this isn't a full frame lens, but with the a7 III, with the crop factor

00:04:31.680 --> 00:04:33.320
this will automatically adjust.

00:04:33.540 --> 00:04:36.660
You can use this lens with this camera, and I love it because it's an inexpensive lens,

00:04:36.770 --> 00:04:41.470
and it gets the job done for vlogging, and it makes this camera super, super light.

00:04:41.470 --> 00:04:43.749
Now, we're gonna move on to my little suitcase here.

00:04:44.000 --> 00:04:50.229
Depending upon what event I'm going to or I don't know where I'm travelling to, I do pack differently.

00:04:50.720 --> 00:04:56.139
But most of these things are pretty much everything that I would normally bring with me, anyway. Usually I won't bring this many lenses,

00:04:56.139 --> 00:05:00.129
I usually just bring one or two. So here we've got my laptop in here.

00:05:00.130 --> 00:05:04.719
Here, all of the Zhiyun crane accessories that I couldn't put in my checked luggage.

00:05:04.760 --> 00:05:10.329
I like to keep one bag easily accessible with all of my hard drives and things that I might need if I'm editing on the plane.

00:05:10.330 --> 00:05:15.190
So I have a bunch of this PC cables that I use for my hard drives.

00:05:15.500 --> 00:05:18.519
These are the samsung solid state drives. These are each two terabytes.

00:05:18.520 --> 00:05:25.180
I basically edit all of my footage off of these, so I can switch between my MacBook, and then editing on my iMac Pro.

00:05:25.180 --> 00:05:30.860
So if i'm editing on my MacBook while I'm travelling and just plug one of these into my iMac Pro and export and it's so much quicker.

00:05:31.060 --> 00:05:33.580
And then I have a 4 TB LaCie drive.

00:05:33.580 --> 00:05:39.300
I usually use this just to back up any footage in case something happens.

00:05:39.580 --> 00:05:44.660
And of course our dongle. This is a little LED light. This is actually the same light that I'm using right here.

00:05:44.920 --> 00:05:46.460
Beautiful.

00:05:46.469 --> 00:05:51.709
Nick was the first one to ever tell us about these, and now Jenna and I have been absolutely obsessed.

00:05:51.710 --> 00:05:53.710
It comes in this cute little bag,

00:05:53.939 --> 00:06:00.679
charges with micro USB. And it even has some filters, and it's got like a little mount on it, too.

00:06:00.680 --> 00:06:03.560
(Jenna: I lost my mount.)
Oh, no!
(Jenna: It's very tragic.)

00:06:03.840 --> 00:06:10.219
We got the DJI Mavic Air. This has been my favorite drone, as of recently. It's super small,

00:06:10.220 --> 00:06:14.360
it's super compact, and the best part about it is the controller - the little joysticks - those come off

00:06:14.360 --> 00:06:17.960
so it's so much easier to travel with. Beautiful drone.

00:06:18.160 --> 00:06:22.820
I feel like I keep everything very, very separate and in little tiny bags.

00:06:23.040 --> 00:06:29.520
This is my Sony RX100 V battery charger. This is a third-party one.

00:06:29.720 --> 00:06:35.360
Here's the RX100 V. Yes, I know it's unrealistic that I'm going to be able to use all of these cameras at the same time.

00:06:35.360 --> 00:06:39.480
But the one time that I won't bring one you'll need it. I like to travel with a mouse.

00:06:39.680 --> 00:06:46.180
I had been recently traveling with a PC as well because Jenna and I have been playing fortnite. So we had been playing on the PCs.

00:06:46.289 --> 00:06:53.179
So I was using this Razer gaming mouse. And we have this little incase bag. This is where I keep all my wires and cables,

00:06:53.729 --> 00:06:59.598
charging bricks. This is basically the battery bag. We've got the GoPro charger. We've got a bunch of cables.

00:06:59.610 --> 00:07:01.909
Plus I got the Apple watch charger, dongles,

00:07:02.729 --> 00:07:04.649
gizmos a-plenty.

00:07:04.649 --> 00:07:09.229
This here is my DJI Mavic charger, also separate.

00:07:09.440 --> 00:07:16.200
Everything has a home. My entire life is usually in disarray, but I can promise you when I'm travelling everything has a place.

